<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador net reserves up to $1.796 bln on Nov 8.</title>
<headline>Ecuador net reserves up to $1.796 bln on Nov 8.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said on Friday that its net international reserves stood at $1.796 billion in the week to November 8, up $23 million from the previous week.</p>
<p>In the week to November 1, international reserves grew $45 million.</p>
<p>The Central Bank did not give an explanation for the growth. International reserves ended 1995 at $1.556 billion.</p>
<p>--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
